OL,3,AScammers demand ransoms from Instagram
OL,4,Ausers over fake copyright claims
OL,5,
OL,6,FInstagram creators say they have lost
OL,7,Fthousands of pounds after their
OL,8,Faccounts were suspended or taken down
OL,9,Fdue to fake copyright claims.
OL,11,FExtorters have filed bogus claims to
OL,12,Fthe Meta-owned social media platform,
OL,13,Fthen asked for ransoms to withdraw them
OL,14,F- knowing repeated claims can lead to
OL,15,Faccount bans.
OL,17,FOne Instagram user, who has 1.5 million
OL,18,Ffollowers, told the BBC he paid a
OL,19,Fscammer $50 (#37) to get his account
OL,20,Fback, claiming Meta's appeal process
OL,21,Fwould take weeks, which had previously
OL,22,Fcost him thousands in lost income.
OL,23,APub: 08-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG5/19
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
